{"step_index":336,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T19:44:38Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-12T21:44:38+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-12T21:44:38+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/Madziva/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/qualification-verification-system/README.md`\nTotal Lines: 135\nTotal Bytes: 6007\nShowing lines 1 to 135\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # DevOps-Enabled Qualification Verification System (QVS)\n2: \n3: [![Build Status](https://img.shields.io/badge/CI%2FCD-GitHub_Actions-blue.svg)](https://github.com)\n4: [![Java Version](https://img.shields.io/badge/Java-17%20%2F%2021-orange.svg)](https://www.oracle.com/java/)\n5: [![Spring Boot](https://img.shields.io/badge/Spring%20Boot-3.2.3-green.svg)](https://spring.io/projects/spring-boot)\n6: [![Coverage](https://img.shields.io/badge/JaCoCo_Coverage->80%25-brightgreen.svg)](target/site/jacoco/index.html)\n7: [![Docker](https://img.shields.io/badge/Docker-Ready-2496ED.svg)](Dockerfile)\n8: [![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-Apache%202.0-blue.svg)](LICENSE)\n9: \n10: An enterprise-grade, DevOps-enabled **Academic and Professional Qualification Verification System** developed with **Java Spring Boot**, containerized with **Docker**, and continuously integrated and delivered via automated **GitHub Actions CI/CD pipelines**.\n11: \n12: ---\n13: \n14: ## 📑 Table of Contents\n15: 1. [Key Features & Capabilities](#-key-features--capabilities)\n16: 2. [DevOps & Software Quality Architecture](#-devops--software-quality-architecture)\n17: 3. [System Architecture Diagram](#-system-architecture-diagram)\n18: 4. [Prerequisites & Quick Start](#-prerequisites--quick-start)\n19: 5. [Automated Testing & Quality Gates](#-automated-testing--quality-gates)\n20: 6. [CI/CD Pipeline Details](#-cicd-pipeline-details)\n21: 7. [Docker & Container Orchestration](#-docker--container-orchestration)\n22: 8. [API Documentation (OpenAPI / Swagger)](#-api-documentation-openapi--swagger)\n23: 9. [Pre-Seeded Demo Accounts](#-pre-seeded-demo-accounts)\n24: 10. [Academic Submission Deliverables](#-academic-submission-deliverables)\n25: \n26: ---\n27: \n28: ## 🌟 Key Features & Capabilities\n29: \n30: - **Tamper-Evident Digital Fingerprinting (Bonus Feature)**: Every qualification is bound to a deterministic SHA-256 cryptographic signature that immediately detects forged or modified credential records.\n31: - **Public & Institutional Verification Portal**: Instant, transparent credential lookup with visual genuine/revoked/tampered badges.\n32: - **Immutable Audit Logging**: Automatic recording of all verification activities, IP addresses, client signatures, and verification outcomes for compliance and forensics.\n33: - **Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)**: Secure JWT authentication with `ROLE_ADMIN`, `ROLE_INSTITUTION`, and `ROLE_VERIFIER`.\n34: - **Credential Lifecycle Management**: Issue, update, search, and revoke qualifications with recorded revocation audit reasons.\n35: \n36: ---\n37: \n38: ## 🛠 DevOps & Software Quality Architecture\n39: \n40: ```mermaid\n41: flowchart LR\n42:     Dev[Developer] -->|Git Flow / PR| GitHub[Git Repository]\n43:     GitHub -->|Webhook Trigger| CI[GitHub Actions CI]\n44:     CI -->|Static Analysis| Checkstyle[Checkstyle Rules]\n45:     CI -->|Automated Tests| Tests[JUnit 5 & Mockito]\n46:     CI -->|Quality Gate| Coverage[JaCoCo >80% Gate]\n47:     CI -->|Container Build| Docker[Docker Multi-Stage]\n48:     Docker -->|Deployment| Prod[Container Runtime / Compose]\n49: ```\n50: \n51: - **Branching Strategy**: Standard GitFlow model (`main`, `develop`, `feature/*`, `bugfix/*`).\n52: - **Static Code Analysis**: Maven Checkstyle plugin enforcing strict Java coding standards.\n53: - **Code Coverage Gate**: JaCoCo Maven plugin enforcing minimum line coverage thresholds.\n54: - **Continuous Deployment**: Multi-stage, minimal attack surface JRE Docker image with non-root security execution.\n55: \n56: ---\n57: \n58: ## 🚀 Prerequisites & Quick Start\n59: \n60: ### Option 1: Run Locally with Maven & Java 17+\n61: ```bash\n62: # Clone the repository\n63: git clone <your-repository-url>\n64: cd qualification-verification-system\n65: \n66: # Run tests and verify build\n67: mvn clean test\n68: \n69: # Launch the Spring Boot application (Dev Profile / In-Memory H2 DB)\n70: mvn spring-boot:run\n71: ```\n72: The application will be accessible at: **`http://localhost:8080`**\n73: \n74: ### Option 2: Run with Docker Compose (PostgreSQL Production Setup)\n75: ```bash\n76: docker compose up --build\n77: ```\n78: This boots both the **Spring Boot application** and a dedicated **PostgreSQL 15** database container.\n79: \n80: ---\n81: \n82: ## 🧪 Automated Testing & Quality Gates\n83: \n84: Run the comprehensive unit and integration test suite:\n85: ```bash\n86: # Execute unit and integration tests\n87: mvn clean test\n88: \n89: # Generate JaCoCo code coverage report\n90: mvn jacoco:report\n91: ```\n92: *Coverage reports are generated at `target/site/jacoco/index.html`.*\n93: \n94: Verify coding standard compliance:\n95: ```bash\n96: mvn checkstyle:check\n97: ```\n98: \n99: ---\n100: \n101: ## 📊 Pre-Seeded Demo Accounts & Records\n102: \n103: The system automatically initializes test accounts and sample certificates on launch:\n104: \n105: ### Demo User Accounts:\n106: | Role | Username | Password | Purpose |\n107: | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n108: | **System Admin** | `admin` | `Admin@12345` | Revoke credentials, manage system |\n109: | **Registrar Officer** | `officer` | `Officer@12345` | Issue & register new qualifications |\n110: \n111: ### Pre-Seeded Sample Qualifications:\n112: | Certificate Number | Graduate Name | Award Title | Status |\n113: | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n114: | `QVS-2024-BSC-8891` | Sarah Jenkins | BSc in Software Engineering | **ACTIVE (Genuine)** |\n115: | `QVS-2023-MSC-4412` | David Miller | MSc in Cybersecurity | **ACTIVE (Genuine)** |\n116: | `QVS-2022-DIP-1109` | Marcus Vance | Diploma in Enterprise Systems | **REVOKED (Disciplinary)** |\n117: \n118: ---\n119: \n120: ## 📖 API Documentation (OpenAPI / Swagger)\n121: \n122: Interactive API documentation with live execution capabilities is available at:\n123: - **Swagger UI**: [http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui.html](http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui.html)\n124: - **OpenAPI JSON**: [http://localhost:8080/api-docs](http://localhost:8080/api-docs)\n125: \n126: ---\n127: \n128: ## 📂 Academic Submission Deliverables\n129: \n130: - 📄 **[Technical Report Template](docs/TECHNICAL_REPORT_TEMPLATE.md)**: Structured 3,000–4,000 word academic report template.\n131: - 🤝 **[Git & GitHub Collaboration Guide](docs/GIT_COLLABORATION_GUIDE.md)**: Team branching strategy, PR workflow, and setup instructions.\n132: - 🎤 **[Viva Presentation & Demo Script](docs/VIVA_DEMO_SCRIPT.md)**: 10–15 minute presentation guide with slide outline.\n133: - 👥 **[Individual Contribution Guide](docs/INDIVIDUAL_CONTRIBUTION_GUIDE.md)**: Contribution evidence report template for team members.\n134: \n135: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
